-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Payroll summaries
--
-- P1 (2026-01, MONTHLY):
--   DEU: E01 = 4000, E02 = 3000, E03 = 2000, E04 = 1000       -> 4 emp, min 1000, max 4000
--   GBR: E05 = 7000 USD, E06 = 6000 USD,
--        E07 = 1000 GBP (= 5000 USD), E25 = 2000 GBP (= 10000 USD)
--         -> 4 emp, USD min 5000, USD max 10000
--         -> GBP identity (only the two GBP rows survive): min 1000, max 2000
--   USA: E08 = 10000, E09 = 9000, E10 = 8000                  -> 3 emp, min 8000, max 10000
--   Global USD: total 55000.00 + 4000.00 = 59000.00? No —
--     the sum shown below is 10000 (DEU) + 28000 (GBR, USD-equivalent)
--     + 27000 (USA) = 65000.00? Recompute from the rows:
--     E01 4000, E02 3000, E03 2000, E04 1000, E05 7000, E06 6000,
--     E07 (GBP 1000 -> USD 5000), E08 10000, E09 9000, E10 8000,
--     E25 (GBP 2000 -> USD 10000) = 65000.00 across 11 employees.
--   NOTE: this is 11 employees, not 10. See "employee count" comment below.
--
-- P2 (2026-02, MONTHLY, FRA): E11 USD 1000, E12 EUR 500 (= USD 1000),
--   E13 XYZ 3000 (dropped). Global: min 1000, max 1000, 2 employees.
--
-- P3 (2026-03, MONTHLY, FRA): E11 EUR 2000 (= USD 4000). Single row.
--
-- P4 (2026-04): empty.
-- P5 (2026-05): only DRAFT rows (excluded by the VALIDATED filter).
--
-- P6 (2026-06, BI_WEEKLY):
--   GBR: E14 8000, E15 7000, E16 6000, E17 6000, E18 5000 -> 5 emp, min 5000, max 8000
--   USA: E19 7000, E20 8000, E21 6000 -> 3 emp, min 6000, max 8000
--   Global: 8 emp, min 5000, max 8000, total 53000.00
--
-- P7 (2026-07, MONTHLY, IND noise): E22 1100, E23 1300, E24 1500.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
